1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,348
Diversification means spreading
investments instead of depending

2
00:00:04,348 --> 00:00:06,250
on one company or one asset.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:10,070
It can reduce the damage caused
by one investment performing

4
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:13,762
badly, but it cannot guarantee
that losses will not occur.

5
00:00:13,762 --> 00:00:17,601
Startup investments are
especially uncertain, and several

6
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:21,574
companies may face similar risks,
such as a weak economy or

7
00:00:21,574 --> 00:00:23,325
limited access to funding.

8
00:00:23,325 --> 00:00:28,109
Consider a simple fictional
illustration: someone puts $1,000

9
00:00:28,109 --> 00:00:30,070
into one startup and that

10
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:33,050
company fails, losing the full
$1,000.

11
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:35,506
Another person divides $1,000

12
00:00:35,506 --> 00:00:38,725
equally across ten unrelated
startups.

13
00:00:38,725 --> 00:00:43,158
If one fails completely and the
other nine merely return the

14
00:00:43,158 --> 00:00:47,665
original $100 each, the second
person would have $900, before

15
00:00:47,665 --> 00:00:49,512
fees and any tax effects.

16
00:00:49,512 --> 00:00:53,507
Real outcomes can be better or
worse, and the companies may

17
00:00:53,507 --> 00:00:55,200
not be truly independent.

18
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,638
Diversification does not make an
unsuitable investment suitable.

19
00:00:59,638 --> 00:01:03,380
Think about your overall
finances, emergency savings,

20
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,900
time horizon, and concentration
across industries and companies.

21
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,607
Do not confuse owning several
startup securities with a

22
00:01:11,607 --> 00:01:13,224
balanced financial plan.

